@@ -9,6 +9,30 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Navigation readiness
+
+Pages use native cross-document view transitions. The shared stylesheet opts in
+on every page and disables transitions for reduced motion. Unsupported browsers
+use standard document navigation.
+
+Keep critical styles in the shared layout's `<head>` so they block rendering.
+The layout's `rel="expect"` link waits for `main-content` by default. Long pages
+set `transitionReadyId="initial-view-ready"` and place that checkpoint immediately
+after their initial content, before below-the-fold sections. The checkpoint only
+waits for HTML parsing, not image loading or React hydration.
+
+The initial layout is server-rendered and currently needs no JavaScript to settle.
+If a page adds JavaScript that changes the initial theme or layout, put it in the
+layout's `head` slot with explicit render blocking, for example:
+
+```astro
+<script slot="head" is:inline type="module" blocking="render" src="/critical-layout.js"></script>
+```
+
+Keep these scripts small and complete their layout work during execution; a
+timer, fetch callback, or unawaited import can run after the render block releases.
+Analytics, ads, and interaction-only hydration must remain non-blocking.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
